# f1 = total, f2 = User, f5 = use
# The end of a class's constructor is two blocks that hold a jump and a return: all its operations stand in its entry block. Where the guard of its copy fails in a loop, it is walked in line once more with the
# parameter unknown: the reads by name at their sites. Nobody but the copy reads the object, so neither walk makes it: its fields are values. Where one of them is no text or number as its use asks, the helper around is called.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = GetSlotOrUndefined {{*}}key="id" receivers=[L1] level=Proven
# CHECK: = GetSlotOrUndefined {{*}}key="active" receivers=[L1] level=Proven
# CHECK: = CallDirect {{*}}function=f5 [isNeverInlined]
# RUN(MADE): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# MADE: code f1:Body
# MADE-NOT: = NewObject
